{"id":49,"text":"A terrible drought hit a farming village. For six months, there was no rain. The crops died, and the animals were thin and weak.\n\nThe villagers invited a famous rain maker from the city. He arrived on a donkey, carrying a large bag. “I can bring rain,” he said. “But I need complete silence and one week of work.”\n\nFor seven days, he sat alone in a hut. Nobody was allowed to enter. He didn’t eat or drink much.\n\nOn the eighth day, dark clouds appeared in the sky, and a heavy rain began to fall. The villagers cheered and danced in the mud.\n\n“How did you do it?” they asked. “What is your secret?”\n\nThe rain maker smiled. “I didn’t make the rain,” he said. “I don’t have magic powers. But when I arrive in a village, I wait until the weather changes. And when I come into a place that is full of worry, I first calm myself. Then I wait.”\n\n“But the rain came after you!” said an old farmer.\n\n“I came after the rain was already on its way,” said the man. “Sometimes, when we are patient and calm, things happen naturally.”\n\nHe took his bag and left the village before anyone could argue.\n\nMoral: Patience and calm can solve many problems that fear and panic cannot.","tr":null,"gl":{"a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","terrible":"dahshatli","drought":"qurg'oqchilik","hit":"urdi","farming":"dehqonchilik","village":"qishloq","for":"uchun; davomida","six":"olti","months":"oylar","there":"u yerda; bor","was":"edi","no":"yo'q; hech qanday","rain":"yomg'ir","the":"(aniq artikl)","crops":"hosil","died":"vafot etdi","and":"va","animals":"hayvonlar","were":"edi(lar)","thin":"ingichka","weak":"zaif","villagers":"qishloq ahli","invited":"taklif qildi","famous":"mashhur","maker":"yasovchi usta","from":"-dan","city":"shahar","he":"u (erkak)","arrived":"yetib keldi","on":"ustida, -da","donkey":"eshak","carrying":"ko'tarib","large":"katta","bag":"sumka","i":"men","can":"qila olmoq","bring":"olib kelmoq","said":"dedi","but":"lekin, ammo","need":"kerak; muhtoj bo'lmoq","complet